; A body falling through a power-law atmosphere with drag, with its
; variational equations: the altitude alt, the speed v and the mass m,
; d/dt alt = v, d/dt v = -g + k * pow(1 + alt / H, -4.5) * v * abs(v) and
; d/dt m = -c * pown(v, 3), the shape of the density laws of JB2008 and
; NRLMSISE-00 (the study, docs/studies/M3-pow.md, section 7's reference;
; the sign of k is the study's), with one tangent vector stepped beside the
; state by the same program. Two of the math library's power routines are
; in its step - pow with a non-integer constant exponent and a
; state-dependent base, and pown with the constant n = 3 - and their rules
; in the tangent (M3's build; the study's section 7): pow's
; (-4.5 * pow(a, -5.5)) * da, whose exponent -5.5 is a pow of its own that
; the primal does not hold, and pown's (3 * pown(v, 2)) * dv, whose
; pown(v, 2) the compiler writes as the product v * v (so the compiled
; bytes hold a multiplication where the graph holds a pown). It is
; compiled round rdn, every rounded operation toward negative infinity,
; where the rules' roundings, written in another shape, are other bytes.
; The run keeps the base 1 + alt / H positive (alt in [0, 4], H = 8) and no
; lane on a structured case of the pow family (an exact power, the zeros
; and the infinities), which would mark by design: leg G fails a segment
; that marks one.
system atmosphere
format fp64
round  rdn
state  alt, v, m
tangent w
param  g = 5/4, H = 8, k = 1/16, c = 1/32
d/dt alt = v
d/dt v = -g + k * pow(1 + alt / H, -4.5) * v * abs(v)
d/dt m = -(c * pown(v, 3))
step   rk4, h = 1/64
